-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",349,{
[11137]="7002EE64\n1\tFind someone near the hidden boat who may know something about it\tSomeone nearby may know something about the boat hidden away from the shore near Parth Galen.\n",
[11138]="70057F5C\n1\tThe members of the Cloudyheads can be found throughout the Blue Theatre in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Duillam has asked you to find and direct the members of the Cloudyheads to the stage in the Blue Theatre.\t\n2\tTalk to Duillam\tDuillam can be found in the Blue Theatre in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have done your best to direct the members of the Cloudyheads to the stage of the Blue Theatre. You should talk to Duillam.\n",
[11139]="70027F4E\n1\tDefeat pit-worms (total: 12)\tPit-worms can be found in the Orc-mines. Meriun asked you to clear several of the scavenging pit-worms out of the mine to help relieve the fears of the Dunlending slaves.\n2\tTalk to Meriun in the Orc-mines\tMeriun is in the Orc-mines. You should tell Meriun that you have slain most of the pit-worms that have terrorized his people.\n",
[11140]="700281D9\n1\tTalk to Bledhun at his camp in the Bonevales\tBledhun is at his encampment in the north-east part of the Bonevales. Bledhun will wish to see this sword.\n",
[11141]="7006989C\n1\tRetrieve dead fish from the shore to the south-west ([see journal]/4)\tRukân asked you to inspect the dead fish that have washed up on the shore to the south-west.\n2\tRetrieve dead fish from the shore to the south-west (3/4)\tRukân asked you to inspect the dead fish that have washed up on the shore to the south-west.\n3\tBring the dead fish and the unpleasant fish-hook to Rukân south-east of the Mâkhda Khorbo\tRukân is waiting for you to return from the shore with anything you might have discovered about the dead fish.\n4\tTalk to Bôdo in the village of Khûtra\tThe fisherman Bôdo in the village of Khûtra may know something about the unpleasant fish-hook you found.\n5\tFind the box of unpleasant design among the hills to the north-west of Khûtra\tBôdo told you he saw a box with similar decorations to the unpleasant fish-hook among the hills to the north-west of Khûtra.\n6\tSearch the box of unpleasant design among the hills north-west of Khûtra\tYou found the box Bôdo described among the hills north-west of Khûtra, and should now search it for some clue to its purpose.\n7\tRecover stolen fish-hooks from goblins or their Corsair allies (total: 8)\tGoblins or their Corsair allies must have taken away the contents of the box. You should recover as many of the cruel fish-hooks as you can.\n8\tBring the stolen fish-hooks to Bôdo in the village of Khûtra\tBôdo will be glad to have the fish-hooks out of the hands of the goblins and their corsair allies, even if it means he must now dispose of the unpleasant artifacts.\n9\tTalk to Rukân east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl\tRukân is east of the Mâkhda Khorbo, north-west of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[11142]="70017613\n1\tReturn the barrel to Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect a barrel of fungus (quantity: see journal)\tOrc fungus-collectors can be found at the Foundations of Stone, south-east of the twenty-first Hall. Veúlfur is at the Twenty-first Hall. Veúlfur wants you to be prepared for the undertaking he intends for you and asked you to retrieve a barrel from the Orc fungus-collectors as the first step in your preparations.\n",
[11143]="7004CE22\n1\tFind the Beornings\tThe Beornings are lost somewhere in Eryn Lasgalen, north of the path. You should find the Beornings.\n2\tTalk to Langhár\tYou have found Langhár alone in a glade north of the path. You should talk to Langhár.\n3\tDefeat Taurogrim (total: 5)\tLanghár is being ambushed by wood-trolls! You should defeat the wood-trolls!\n4\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár is in a small glade north of the path in Eryn Lasgalen. You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[11144]="7001C494\n1\tBring the glinting signet-ring to Narthan\030Find the glinting signet-ring (quantity: see journal)\tNarthan's ring might be found upon one of the wights roaming west of Ost Haer. Narthan told you of his wife, her passing, and the ring that he carried during his life to remind him of the woman. He asked that you find it for him.\n",
[11145]="70054F2C\n1\tTravel to Taen Orwath\tTaen Orwath can be found in the southern eastern hills of Rath Dúath. Candúr has asked you to travel to Taen Orwath and aid the Rangers of Ithilien preparing to venture into Thuringwath.\n2\tTalk to Cuilion\tCuilion can be found at Taen Orwath. One of the Rangers at Taen Orwath appears to have been awaiting your arrival. You should talk to Cuilion.\n",
[11146]="70026194\n1\tPour the phial into the water\030Reach the pool below the Twisted Grove\tThe Twisted Grove is south-west of the Eavespires. Remmenylf asked you to go to the Twisted Grove and pour the Ent's tear into the pool beneath it.\n2\tTalk to Remmenylf at the Eavespires\tRemmenylf is at the Eavespires, north-east of the Twisted Grove. Remmenylf will be dismayed to hear that the Ent's tears did not purify the waters.\n",
[11147]="7002818D\n1\tTalk to Andras' son at his farmstead\tAndras' homestead is in the north-west of the Starkmoor. Andras asked you go to his homestead and give the ledger to his son.\n",
[11148]="70072E79\n1\tSearch to the east\tYou have come to the Crypts of Gadim-ûn to search for a sign of what may have caused the dead to rise in An Shêru. You should start by searching to the east.\n2\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have found a corrupted corpse surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Perhaps you should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n3\tSearch for another clue further east\tAfter finding a corrupted corpse, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should continue east and search the crypts for anything else notable.\n4\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have found another corrupted corpse. You should sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers, as you did last time.\n5\tSearch for another sign to the south\tAfter finding two corrupted corpses, you were able to dispel the foul voice in the air with a lighthearted song. You should travel south and continue searching the crypts.\n6\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have discovered a third corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n7\tSearch for another clue to the west\tYou have now found three corrupted corpses, each surrounded by a green radiance and the sound of a tormented voice. Each time, you were able to dispel the foul voice with a lighthearted song. You should travel west and continue searching the crypts.\n8\tSoothe the anguished dead\tYou have found yet another corrupted corpse. You should again sing a lighthearted song to yourself to ward off the fell whispers.\n",
[11149]="70017587\n1\tPlay a song for Erling Goodbody in Bree\tErling Goodbody can be found in the thoroughfare in front of the Prancing Pony. Pada, a widely-respected Minstrel, has asked you to cheer a friend of his from Bree using the great instrument you recently recovered.\n2\tSpeak with Erling Goodbody\tSpeak with Erling and let him know that Pada sends his best.\n3\tReturn to Pada\tPada is in the Foundations of Stone in Moria. You should return to Pada and tell him that his friend Erling Goodbody was very pleased with the song you played.\n",
[11150]="70018FCF\n1\tTalk to Orthir\tOrthir can be found a short distance west of Cerin Amroth, near the path. Mallendathor wishes you to speak to Orthir, the Scholar of the Trees, to see if he knows what might heal the saplings' malady.\n2\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (0/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n3\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (1/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n4\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (2/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n5\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (3/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n6\tTalk to Sendiel in Gelirdor\tSendiel is in Gelirdor, south-west of the Malbrethil-trees, east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir instructed you to tell Sendiel of your success.\n",
[11151]="70041A78\n1\tTalk to Faltharan in Pelargir\tFaltharan can be found somewhere in Pelargir. Nimithil has grown concerned for her husband after hearing news of a great battle in Pelargir. You should seek out Faltharan.\n",
[11152]="70041A4D\n1\tTalk to Erchar\tErchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Jajax has asked you to rally Garvir's brothers to Hata Kebir so they may seek vengeance against Azgarzôr.\n2\tTalk to Nimithil\tNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed. After dispatching Azgarzôr, Erchar and Herion suggested you return to the people of Lebennin. You should speak to Nimithil.\n",
[11153]="70071604\n1\tSpeak with Elder Jurmêna to obtain the salve\tSpeak with Elder Jurmêna to obtain the salve for injured cattle.\n2\tGive salve to Blossom\030Give salve to Biscuit\030Give salve to Bela\030Give salve to Butters\030Give salve to Bailey\tGive the salve to injured cattle in Sormedân.\n3\tReturn to Lurâkha in Sormedân\tReturn to Lurâkha in Sormedân with news of the effects of the salve on her cattle.\n",
[11154]="7004799C\n1\tDefeat Black Númenórean sorcerers (total: 4)\tBlack Númenórean sorcerers can be found within the Towers of the Teeth. You should defeat Black Númenórean sorcerers.\n2\tReturn to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr, who can be found at a small Ranger outpost hidden in the Slag-hills.\n",
[11155]="7004AF9D\n1\tDefeat Sorcerers (total: 3)\tDefeat Easterling Sorcerers in Rhûd Vorn.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated Easterling Sorcerers in Rhûd Vorn.\n",
[11156]="7003E735\n1\tDefeat Gauradan-ritualists\tGauradan-ritualists can be found at Echad Gaurdan, south of Echad Candelleth. You should defeat the Gauradan-ritualists, removing the threat they pose to those who dwell in Tâl Bruinen.\n2\tDefeat Gauradan-ritualists (total: 3)\tGauradan-ritualists can be found at Echad Gaurdan, south of Echad Candelleth. You should defeat the Gauradan-ritualists, removing the threat they pose to those who dwell in Tâl Bruinen.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the Gauradan-ritualists, removing the threat they pose to those who dwell in Tâl Bruinen.\n",
[11157]="7000A16D\n1\tDefeat Múlvuirë, High Sorceress\030Defeat Afraig, Gúlaran Sorceress\030Defeat Coblaith, Gúlaran Sorceress\tFind the three Sorceresses within Barad Gúlaran and defeat them. If they are stopped, then there will be no others to carry out the will of Amarthiel. Brúnfair asked you to search through the halls of Barad Gúlaran in search of the sorceresses left in charge of carrying out Amarthiel's will. Find them and destroy them.\n2\tTalk to Brúnfair\tYou have defeated the sorceresses within Barad Gúlaran. Return to Brúnfair at the Ranger encampment in the north-eastern section of Angmar and tell him of your success. Searching through the halls of Barad Gúlaran you discovered and defeated the sorceresses responsible for carrying out the machinations of Amarthiel in Angmar.\n",
[11158]="7002D4E5\n1\tFind Sori in the southern tunnels\tSori travelled south from Menem-berej, and should be found somewhere in the tunnel leading south through the Silvertine Lodes. You should find Sori and offer him your assistance.\n",
[11159]="7003A5E2\n1\tTalk to Meregyth\tMeregyth stands near Cúthing, outside the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. Cúthing informed you that Meregyth wants to have a word with you before speak with his father.\n2\tTalk to Thane Cútha\tThane Cútha is in the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch. Cúthing told you to speak with his father, Thane Cútha.\n",
[11160]="7000979D\n1\tSort small relics on the mat\030Sort medium relics on the mat\030Sort large relics on the mat\tDifferent-sized relics and bits of pottery are lying on the mats by Astiul at Tinnudir, on Parth Aduial in Evendim. Astiul has asked you to sort the pottery fragments and relics you collected from the shores of Lake Neniul by size on the mats he uses for that purpose.\n2\tReturn satchel of pottery to Astiul\tAstiul is at Tinnudir, on Parth Aduial in Evendim. Ranger Astiul will be pleased that you sorted out the relics and pottery shards you collected from the shores of Lake Nenuial.\n",
[11161]="7002604D\n1\tSort the pipe-weed (total: 3)\tThe pipe-weed barrels are next to Blossom Gamgee. The pipe-weed needs to be sorted before it can be dried.\n2\tTalk to Blossom Gamgee\tBlossom Gamgee is at the Northcotton Farm. Blossom Gamgee will want to know that the pipe-weed has been sorted.\n",
[11162]="7003045C\n1\tFind the missing soldier near Wódscrafen\tNorth of Twickenburg is the highest point in the Wold, Cracabor, and over that hill is the ancient cave of Wódscrafen. You should head to Wódscrafen and search for the soldier who went that way.\n2\tInvestigate the old cave\tNorth of Twickenburg is the highest point in the Wold, Cracabor, and over that hill is the ancient cave of Wódscrafen. You should explore the cave north of Twickenburg.\n3\tFind the root of the disturbance in Wódscrafen\tThe cave of Wódscrafen can be found north of Twickenburg in the Wold. You should explore the cave of Wódscrafen to find out what disturbed the dead there.\n4\tReturn to the frightened soldier\tThe frightened soldier is outside of Wódscrafen in the Wold. You should return to the frightened soldier and tell him of the Ringwraith you saw in Wódscrafen.\n",
[11163]="7006BB5F\n1\tInvestigate the waterfall for an entrance\tEdâkhi has asked you to investigate behind the waterfall for the home of the Idâmi.\n2\tSpeak with Enârshan, the Idâmi\tSpeak with the Idâmi in her home behind the waterfall in Ilûritu.\n",
[11164]="7002291A\n1\tFind the first skeleton pile\030Find the second skeleton pile\030Find the third skeleton pile\tThe barrows Mincham wants you to investigate are located to the east of the road, along the southern border of the Lich Bluffs. Mincham has asked you seek out the entrances to some of the barrows and investigate the corpses of the recently disturbed dead.\n2\tTalk to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs\tMincham is at his camp, north of the barrows. You should return to Mincham and report what you found at the ancient barrows.\n",
[11165]="7001A9AC\n1\tDefeat the half-orc leader in Andrath\tThe half-orc leader can be found just inside the gate from the south in the Vale of Andrath. Watcher Oakdale has asked you to defeat the leader of the half-orcs from the south.\n2\tTalk to Watcher Oakdale\tWatcher Oakdale is at the east edge of the northern part of the Southwatch. You defeated the half-orc leader deep within the enemy camp at Andrath and should now return to Watcher Oakdale.\n",
[11166]="7002EE44\n1\tBurn Orc-tents at Maustazg\t\n2\tBurn Orc-tents at Maustazg (total: 5)\tTents of the enemy can be found at the Orc-camp of Maustazg, east of Eaworth. You should sow mayhem at Maustazg by setting fire to the Orcs' tents.\n3\tTalk to Ingmar in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngmar is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth, west of Maustazg. You should return to Ingmar and let him know what you have done.\n",
[11167]="7002EE47\n1\tBurn Orc-tents at Maustazg\t\n2\tBurn Orc-tents at Maustazg (total: 5)\tOrc-tents can be found at Maustazg, east of Eaworth, in the Entwash Vale. You should take the opportunity to sow mayhem among the Orcs by burning their tents.\n3\tTalk to Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tGóda is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth, west of Maustazg. You should return to Góda and let her know what you have done.\n",
[11168]="7006F08E\n1\tGather seed bags (total: 4)\tGather bags of seeds to help Ashnân plant extra crops in Burukíri.\n2\tPlant seeds (total: 12)\tPlant the seeds in the locations at which the soil has already been tilled around Burukíri.\n3\tReturn to Ashnân in Burukíri\tReturn to Ashnân in Burukíri and inform him that you have planted the crop seeds for him.\n",
})
